       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is about double the maximum recommended daily dose (3200 mg/day, the labeled ceiling for prescription ibuprofen). Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention, even with normal baseline kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon intended regimens would be:\n- **400 mg PO q6h or 600 mg PO q6h** (or q8h), for typical analgesia\n- **800 mg PO q6\u20138h**, up to a maximum of 3200 mg/day for inflammatory conditions\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter the corrected order. If 1600 mg QID is intentional, tell me the indication and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale."
